  "decisions": [
    {
      "concept": "selector",
      "note": "RotarySelector: a cam-lobe selector stepper `selector_stepper: unit0_selector` beside a separate gear drive, declared in `[mmu_unit unit0]`; no servo, no encoder. klipper-mmu drives it as a ROTARY selector (`KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_KIND_ROTARY`) with Happy Hare's HTLF numbers: 32 mm selector rotation distance, 50 mm/s and 50 mm/s^2, release gates `1, 2, 3, 0`. The selector homes to its endstop before the first selection and after a fault, and starts from the quick-calibration positions `4.0,29.0,54.0,79.0` mm until `KLIPPER_MMU_CALIBRATE_SELECTOR` measures the real ones. AFC's HTLF is the same idea with a home endstop, `AFC_HOME_UNIT` and lobe-angle math. Software candidate: it builds and passes the simulators, but has not run on real hardware."
    },
    {
      "concept": "encoder",
      "note": "No encoder declared: `[mmu_unit unit0]` has no `encoder` key and the trace has no `[mmu_encoder]` section, so klipper-mmu's optional encoder input (`KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER`) stays off. HTLF's own AFC templates wire none either."
    },
    {
      "concept": "arrival",
      "note": "AFC `None` vs HH `unit0:mmu_shared_exit`. HH's LOAD's only homing move is the gear homing to the shared-exit switch; the move to the nozzle is dead-reckoned (`extruder_homing_endstop: none`). AFC's toolhead arrival switch is `pin_tool_start: enter_tool_pin` in the separate `templates/AFC_Hardware-HTLF.cfg` (a placeholder), not in the unit template the compare reads, so the AFC side is None. Adopt HH's shared-exit arrival; a real toolhead switch is a gap, not fabricated."
    },
    {
      "concept": "buffer_type",
      "note": "`n/a` in the compare (the AFC unit template has no `[AFC_buffer]`; the HH trace has no `[mmu_buffer unit0]`). AFC's separate `templates/AFC_Hardware-HTLF.cfg:17-21` defines a switched Turtleneck `[AFC_buffer TN]` (`advance_pin`/`trailing_pin` placeholders, multipliers 1.05/0.95), but the unit block names `buffer: Turtle_1` (ERB) / `TurtleNeck` (MMB), which no section defines. Switched-buffer ramming and a single-ended analog PSF frontend are both gaps in klipper-mmu, not blockers."
    },
    {
      "concept": "lane_count",
      "note": "AFC 2 vs HH 4. The AFC count is of `[AFC_stepper]` sections, and HTLF's four `[AFC_lane HTLF_1:n]` blocks carry no step pins -- they borrow the unit drive -- so the AFC-side 2 is the drive plus selector stepper, not a lane count. AFC also configures four lanes (`templates/AFC_HTLF_1-ERB.cfg:61,67,73,79`). Adopt 4: both sides describe a four-lane unit."
    },
    {
      "concept": "hub_sensor",
      "note": "AFC `^ERB:HUB` (gpio25, ERB) / `^MMB_HTLF:HUB` (PC13, MMB) vs HH `^unit0:PA15`. Both declare a real shared-exit/hub switch; the pins differ because HH's trace runs a generic placeholder board while AFC's alias file names the real ERB/MMB pin. Pins are board wiring, not device behaviour, and Happy Hare's placeholders never override a real board's wiring: klipper-mmu binds the switch as `has_hub_sensor` on `KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_HUB`, set to your board's pin (AFC's alias files give the real ERB and MMB pins)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "unload_park",
      "note": "AFC `hub_clear_move_dis: 65` vs HH `gate_parking_distance: -25`. They are not quite the same quantity (AFC's is hub-clearance travel; HH's is the park position behind the shared-exit switch), which is itself the finding. Where they differ, HH's number stands (the executable reference): klipper-mmu adopts 25 mm behind `unit0:mmu_shared_exit`; record AFC's 65 mm clearance."
    },
    {
      "concept": "long_speed",
      "note": "AFC 150/50 (unit `long_moves_speed`/`long_moves_accel`, `templates/AFC_HTLF_1-ERB.cfg:23-24`) vs HH 135/100 (`gear_load_speed`/`gear_load_accel`). Default: adopt HH's 135/100. AFC's selector movement is separate and even slower (its code defaults 50/50 and no template sets them); klipper-mmu's HTLF selector moves at Happy Hare's 50 mm/s and 50 mm/s^2 (`KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_MOVE_SPEED_MM_S`, `KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_ACCEL_MM_S2`)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "short_speed",
      "note": "AFC 50/300 (global `short_moves_speed`/`short_moves_accel`, `config/AFC.cfg:9-10`) vs HH 80/400 (`gear_short_move_speed`/`gear_short_move_accel`). Default: adopt HH's 80/400."
    },
    {
      "concept": "preload_park",
      "note": "AFC None vs HH 25 mm behind `unit0:mmu_shared_exit` (`gate_preload_parking_distance: -25`, `operations.preload.end.tip = -15.0`). HTLF's lanes set no `park_dist` and the hub has no park key, so AFC has no number to weigh; HH stands alone."
    },
    {
      "concept": "eject_extra",
      "note": "AFC None vs HH `gate_final_eject_distance: 20` (tip -35.000001). AFC's HTLF inherits `afcBoxTurtle.eject_lane`, which retracts to the LOAD switch and then steps back hub-length increments -- no explicit extra distance and no selector-aware parking. Adopt HH's 20 mm."
    },
    {
      "concept": "bowden",
      "note": "AFC-only: `afc_bowden_length: 1990.0` (ERB) / `1750` (MMB) vs HH None. HH's `layout` distances are synthetic harness geometry (`variable_bowden_lengths: false`, `require_bowden_move: true`) and hold no real bowden number, so AFC's measured length is the only real number on record. klipper-mmu measures the Bowden itself (`KLIPPER_MMU_CALIBRATE`) and keeps one length per unit -- a per-lane gap, not a blocker."
    }
  ]
}
